  "slug": "injury-cord-c274",
  "summary": "Five preprints release open tools for microglial morphology, single-cell exploration, connectomics and spatial inference of cell-state transitions.",
  "synthesis": "The items share an emphasis on accessible computational tools for resolving cell state and cellular context, with only one addressing microglia directly. PolyMorph3D, an open-source MATLAB tool, quantifies 3D microglia morphology and colocalization with up to four markers in mouse and human tissue. Niche-FATE applies optimal transport that combines expression, spatial neighbourhoods and ligand-receptor signalling to infer cell-state transitions from spatiotemporal data. A kidney spatial transcriptomics study infers networks of interacting subcellular processes across cellular neighborhoods. SingloCell (multimodal single-cell exploration) and Jump (EM connectomics annotation) lower access barriers to large datasets. What is new is the pairing of morphological or spatial-niche readouts with open, browser- or code-based analysis, rather than new biological findings on microglia or macrophage state dynamics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
